   "solution": "1. Open **Monitor > Metrics** and review **Percentage CPU (Average)** for **vm-app-02**.\n2. Select **New alert rule**. On **Scope**, choose **vm-app-02**.\n3. On **Condition**, set **Signal name** **Percentage CPU**, **Threshold type** **Static**, **Aggregation type** **Average**, **Operator** **Greater than**, **Threshold value** `80`, **Check every** **5 minutes**, and **Lookback period** **5 minutes**.\n4. On **Actions**, choose **Create action group** and enter **Action group name** `ag-ops`, **Display name** `OPS`, **Notification type** **Email/SMS message/Push/Voice**, and **Email** `ops@contoso.example`.\n5. On **Details**, set **Severity** **Sev2 - Warning**, **Alert rule name** `alert-vm-app-02-cpu`, keep **Enable upon creation** on, then select **Review + create** and **Create**.\n6. Return to **Monitor > Metrics** and select **Run CPU stress test** or run `run-cpu-stress --vm vm-app-02` in Cloud Shell.\n7. Open **Alerts** and select **Acknowledge** for **High CPU on vm-app-02**.\n8. Open **Service Health** and review how **Service Health** differs from **Resource Health**."
  }
